          "duration": "25 mins",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "# 🟢 Present Indefinite Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + is / am / are + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nIn Present Indefinite (Simple Present), we describe habits, daily routines, facts, and standard operations. When shifted to passive voice, we emphasize the action or the object receiving that action rather than who performs it.\n\n#### Auxiliary Selection:\n- **am:** Used exclusively with first-person singular **'I'** (*e.g., \"I am guided by Dr Wazir.\"*)\n- **is:** Used with singular subjects (*He, She, It, singular noun*) (*e.g., \"Cricket is played.\"*)\n- **are:** Used with plural subjects (*You, We, They, plural nouns*) (*e.g., \"Books are read.\"*)\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + V1(+s/es) + Object` | `Object + is/am/are + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + do/does + not + V1 + Object` | `Object + is/am/are + not + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Do/Does + Subject + V1 + Object + ?` | `Is/Am/Are + Object + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Do/Does + Subject + not + V1 + Object + ?` | `Is/Am/Are + Object + not + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** Farmers harvest wheat in April across Punjab.\n- **Passive:** Wheat is harvested in April across Punjab by farmers.\n- **Active:** She sings melodious ghazals at the festival.\n- **Passive:** Melodious ghazals are sung by her at the festival.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** He does not lock the main entrance gate at night.\n- **Passive:** The main entrance gate is not locked by him at night.\n- **Active:** We do not tolerate examination malpractice.\n- **Passive:** Examination malpractice is not tolerated by us.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Does your father operate this textile machinery?\n- **Passive:** Is this textile machinery operated by your father?\n- **Active:** Do they deliver fresh dairy products every dawn?\n- **Passive:** Are fresh dairy products delivered by them every dawn?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Does the accountant not balance the ledger every evening?\n- **Passive:** Is the ledger not balanced by the accountant every evening?\n- **Active:** Do the authorities not repair these damaged bridges?\n- **Passive:** Are these damaged bridges not repaired by the authorities?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *English is spoke all over the world.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *English is **spoken** all over the world.* (V3 of speak is spoken).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Do novels are read by her?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Are** novels read by her?* (Do/does are replaced by is/am/are in passive voice).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Tea does not taken by him.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *Tea **is not** taken by him.* (Never retain do/does in passive voice).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Apples is eaten by the children.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *Apples **are** eaten by the children.* (Plural object requires 'are').\n",
