          "content": "# 🟢 Present Continuous Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + is / am / are + being + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nWhen an action is currently in progress at the time of speaking, the active voice utilizes `is/am/are + verb-ing`. To preserve the continuous aspect in passive voice, the auxiliary **being** is mandatory between *is/am/are* and the *past participle (V3)*.\n\n#### The Role of \"Being\":\nWithout *being*, a sentence collapses into simple present passive (*\"The house is built\"* means it is completed or habitually built, whereas *\"The house is being built\"* means construction is currently underway).\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + is/am/are + V-ing + Object` | `Object + is/am/are + being + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + is/am/are + not + V-ing + Object` | `Object + is/am/are + not + being + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Is/Am/Are + Subject + V-ing + Object + ?` | `Is/Am/Are + Object + being + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Is/Am/Are + Subject + not + V-ing + Object + ?` | `Is/Am/Are + Object + not + being + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** The technicians are repairing the fiber optic cable.\n- **Passive:** The fiber optic cable is being repaired by the technicians.\n- **Active:** Mother is cooking delicious chicken biryani for the guests.\n- **Passive:** Delicious chicken biryani is being cooked for the guests by mother.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The students are not making noise in the examination hall.\n- **Passive:** Noise is not being made by the students in the examination hall.\n- **Active:** The contractor is not paving the secondary roads.\n- **Passive:** The secondary roads are not being paved by the contractor.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Is the doctor examining the emergency patient?\n- **Passive:** Is the emergency patient being examined by the doctor?\n- **Active:** Are the scouts pitching the tents on the hillside?\n- **Passive:** Are the tents being pitched on the hillside by the scouts?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Is she not writing the research abstract right now?\n- **Passive:** Is the research abstract not being written by her right now?\n- **Active:** Are they not televising the cricket semi-final live?\n- **Passive:** Is the cricket semi-final not being televised live by them?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The bridge is repairing by the team.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The bridge **is being repaired** by the team.* (Omitting 'being' and V3 turns the bridge into the doer).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *A song is been sung by Fatima.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *A song is **being** sung by Fatima.* ('Been' is for Perfect tenses; 'being' is for Continuous tenses).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Is being the question answered by the teacher?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Is the question being answered** by the teacher?* ('Being' must follow the object in interrogative sentences).\n",
