          "content": "# 🟢 Present Perfect Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + has / have + been + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nThe Present Perfect Tense expresses actions completed recently or past actions with present consequences. In passive voice, the word **been** is inserted between the auxiliary *has/have* and the *past participle (V3)*.\n\n#### Subject-Verb Agreement:\n- **has been:** For singular objects (*He, She, It, singular noun*)\n- **have been:** For plural objects (*I, We, You, They, plural nouns*)\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + has/have + V3 + Object` | `Object + has/have + been + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + has/have + not + V3 + Object` | `Object + has/have + not + been + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Has/Have + Subject + V3 + Object + ?` | `Has/Have + Object + been + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Has/Have + Subject + not + V3 + Object + ?` | `Has/Have + Object + not + been + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** The Ministry of Education has announced the revised academic calendar.\n- **Passive:** The revised academic calendar has been announced by the Ministry of Education.\n- **Active:** Pakistan has produced world-class cricket legends.\n- **Passive:** World-class cricket legends have been produced by Pakistan.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The administration has not published the merit list yet.\n- **Passive:** The merit list has not been published by the administration yet.\n- **Active:** We have not received the dispatched consignment.\n- **Passive:** The dispatched consignment has not been received by us.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Have you solved all algebraic equations accurately?\n- **Passive:** Have all algebraic equations been solved accurately by you?\n- **Active:** Has the surgeon performed the complex heart surgery?\n- **Passive:** Has the complex heart surgery been performed by the surgeon?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Has he not submitted the tax declaration on time?\n- **Passive:** Has the tax declaration not been submitted by him on time?\n- **Active:** Have they not finalized the tournament venues?\n- **Passive:** Have the tournament venues not been finalized by them?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The homework has finished by Ali.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The homework **has been finished** by Ali.* (Without 'been', the homework is grammatically depicted as finishing itself).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The parcel have been delivered.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The parcel **has been** delivered.* (Singular parcel requires 'has been').\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Have been the cars washed by him?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Have the cars been** washed by him?* ('Been' must follow the subject in questions).\n",
