          "type": "text",
          "content": "# 🟢 Present Perfect Continuous: Passive Analysis\n\n> **Theoretical Formula:** `Object + has/have + been + being + V3 + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Conventional Usage\nIn standard modern English grammar, **Present Perfect Continuous Tense is conventionally NOT used in the passive voice**. \n\n#### Why is it Avoided?\nConstructing the passive requires stacking two forms of the verb *to be* sequentially: **been** + **being**.\n- *Active:* \"The workers have been repairing the highway for three days.\"\n- *Theoretical Passive:* \"The highway **has been being repaired** by the workers for three days.\"\n\nThis dual-be construction (*been being*) creates harsh phonetic dissonance, sounds awkward to native speakers, and leads to clunky prose.\n\n#### What do Grammarians & Style Guides Recommend?\n1. **Retain Active Voice (Preferred):** Keep the sentence in active voice where possible.\n2. **Convert to Present Perfect Passive:** *\"The highway has been repaired by the workers for three days.\"*\n3. **Convert to Present Continuous Passive:** *\"The highway is being repaired by the workers.\"*\n\nNevertheless, competitive examinations (such as CSS, PMS, and Federal Board exams) occasionally test candidates on theoretical formulation.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Theoretical Structural Matrix\n\n| Sentence Type | Theoretical Passive Structure | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Object + has/have + been being + V3` | The manuscript **has been being edited** by him. |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Object + has/have + not + been being + V3` | The parcels **have not been being delivered** properly. |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Has/Have + Object + been being + V3 + ?` | **Has** the project **been being monitored** by the audit team? |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Has/Have + Object + not + been being + V3 + ?` | **Have** the accounts **not been being audited** by them? |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Illustrative Conversions (Theoretical vs Practical)\n\n- **Active:** Dr Wazir has been supervising the research candidates since January.\n  - *Theoretical Passive:* The research candidates have been being supervised by Dr Wazir since January.\n  - *Standard Stylistic Alternative:* The research candidates have been supervised by Dr Wazir since January.\n- **Active:** The contractor has not been maintaining the sports stadium.\n  - *Theoretical Passive:* The sports stadium has not been being maintained by the contractor.\n  - *Standard Stylistic Alternative:* The sports stadium has not been maintained by the contractor.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *He has being reading the book.* (Active mix-up).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The book has been being readen.* ('Readen' is invalid; V3 of read is *read* pronounced /rɛd/).\n- ❌ **Stylistic Error:** Overusing *been being* in natural conversational or formal business English.\n",
