          "content": "# 🟠 Past Continuous Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + was / were + being + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nWhen an action was in progress at a particular juncture in the past, active voice uses `was/were + verb-ing`. To transform this into passive voice while maintaining the progressive past aspect, we combine **was/were** with **being** and the **past participle (V3)**.\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + was/were + V-ing + Object` | `Object + was/were + being + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + was/were + not + V-ing + Object` | `Object + was/were + not + being + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Was/Were + Subject + V-ing + Object + ?` | `Was/Were + Object + being + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Was/Were + Subject + not + V-ing + Object + ?` | `Was/Were + Object + not + being + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** When I visited Lahore, the artisans were restoring the Shahi Qila.\n- **Passive:** When I visited Lahore, the Shahi Qila was being restored by the artisans.\n- **Active:** The chef was preparing dinner when the electricity failed.\n- **Passive:** Dinner was being prepared by the chef when the electricity failed.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The security guards were not monitoring the surveillance cameras.\n- **Passive:** The surveillance cameras were not being monitored by the security guards.\n- **Active:** She was not driving the vehicle at the moment of impact.\n- **Passive:** The vehicle was not being driven by her at the moment of impact.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Were the villagers repairing the canal banks before the flood arrived?\n- **Passive:** Were the canal banks being repaired by the villagers before the flood arrived?\n- **Active:** Was the professor delivering the lecture when the earthquake struck?\n- **Passive:** Was the lecture being delivered by the professor when the earthquake struck?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Was he not distributing relief packages among the affected families?\n- **Passive:** Were relief packages not being distributed among the affected families by him?\n- **Active:** Were they not inspecting the emergency exits?\n- **Passive:** Were the emergency exits not being inspected by them?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The room was cleaning when I entered.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The room **was being cleaned** when I entered.*\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Dinner was been cooked.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *Dinner was **being** cooked.* ('Been' is for Past Perfect, 'being' is for Continuous).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Were being the patients attended?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Were the patients being** attended?*\n",
