          "content": "# 🔵 Future Indefinite Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + will / shall + be + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nFuture Indefinite (Simple Future) denotes actions that will take place in the future. In passive voice, the modal auxiliaries **will** or **shall** are paired with the base verb **be** followed by the **past participle (V3)**.\n\n#### Will vs Shall:\n- In contemporary global English, **will be** is standard and accepted for all subjects (*I, We, You, He, She, It, They*).\n- In traditional formal or legal English, **shall be** is occasionally preserved for first-person (*I/We*) or regulatory mandates (*\"Taxes shall be paid by April 15\"*).\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + will/shall + V1 + Object` | `Object + will/shall + be + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + will/shall + not + V1 + Object` | `Object + will/shall + not + be + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Will/Shall + Subject + V1 + Object + ?` | `Will/Shall + Object + be + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Will/Shall + Subject + not + V1 + Object + ?` | `Will/Shall + Object + not + be + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** The university will award degrees at the annual convocation.\n- **Passive:** Degrees will be awarded by the university at the annual convocation.\n- **Active:** Pakistan Railway will upgrade the mainline track next year.\n- **Passive:** The mainline track will be upgraded by Pakistan Railway next year.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The airline will not cancel international flights due to light rain.\n- **Passive:** International flights will not be cancelled by the airline due to light rain.\n- **Active:** We will not compromise on educational standards.\n- **Passive:** Educational standards will not be compromised by us.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Will the governor inaugurate the new public library?\n- **Passive:** Will the new public library be inaugurated by the governor?\n- **Active:** Will they broadcast the final match worldwide?\n- **Passive:** Will the final match be broadcast worldwide by them?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Will she not notify the shortlisted candidates?\n- **Passive:** Will the shortlisted candidates not be notified by her?\n- **Active:** Won't they deliver the furniture before Saturday?\n- **Passive:** Won't the furniture be delivered by them before Saturday?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The project will finished tomorrow.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The project **will be finished** tomorrow.* (Missing 'be').\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Will be the letter posted by him?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Will the letter be** posted by him?*\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The book will is published next month.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The book **will be published** next month.* (Modal verbs take base 'be', never 'is').\n",
