          "duration": "20 mins",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "# 🔵 Future Continuous Tense: Passive Analysis\n\n> **Theoretical Formula:** `Object + will + be + being + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Conventional Usage\nIn standard English, **Future Continuous Tense is conventionally NOT cast in the passive voice**.\n\n#### Why is it Avoided?\nConstructing passive for future continuous requires pairing modal *will* with **be** and immediately following it with **being**:\n- *Active:* \"At 10 AM tomorrow, the engineers will be testing the turbine.\"\n- *Theoretical Passive:* \"At 10 AM tomorrow, the turbine **will be being tested** by the engineers.\"\n\nThe juxtaposition of **be being** is considered cacophonous and grating in spoken and written English.\n\n#### Recommended Native Alternatives:\n1. **Retain Active Voice (Ideal):** *\"The engineers will be testing the turbine tomorrow.\"*\n2. **Convert to Simple Future Passive:** *\"The turbine will be tested by the engineers tomorrow.\"*\n3. **Convert to an Active Progressive Clause:** *\"Testing of the turbine will be underway tomorrow.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Theoretical Structural Matrix\n\n| Sentence Type | Theoretical Passive Structure | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Object + will be being + V3` | The bridge **will be being painted** next week. |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Object + will not be being + V3` | The cars **will not be being washed** at noon. |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Will + Object + be being + V3 + ?` | **Will** the match **be being played** at that hour? |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Will + Object + not + be being + V3 + ?` | **Will** the files **not be being reviewed** by the auditor? |\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The exam will being taken at 9 AM.* ('Will being' is ungrammatical; modal requires bare 'be').\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The letter will be been sent.* ('Be been' is invalid).\n",
