          "content": "# 📋 Master Cheat Sheet: Active & Passive Voice Across All 12 Tenses\n\n> **The Definitive Quick Reference Compendium** — Dr Wazir Ahmed\n\n---\n\n### 🏛️ Complete 12-Tense Voice Matrix\n\n| # | Tense | Active Voice Structure | Passive Voice Structure | Example Passive |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | **Present Indefinite** | `V1 (+s/es)` | `is / am / are + V3` | The bell **is rung**. |\n| **2** | **Present Continuous** | `is/am/are + V-ing` | `is / am / are + being + V3` | The bell **is being rung**. |\n| **3** | **Present Perfect** | `has/have + V3` | `has / have + been + V3` | The bell **has been rung**. |\n| **4** | **Present Perfect Cont.** | `has/have been + V-ing` | *[Rare]* `has/have been being + V3` | *Avoided in standard English* |\n| **5** | **Past Indefinite** | `V2` | `was / were + V3` | The bell **was rung**. |\n| **6** | **Past Continuous** | `was/were + V-ing` | `was / were + being + V3` | The bell **was being rung**. |\n| **7** | **Past Perfect** | `had + V3` | `had + been + V3` | The bell **had been rung**. |\n| **8** | **Past Perfect Cont.** | `had been + V-ing` | *[Rare]* `had been being + V3` | *Avoided in standard English* |\n| **9** | **Future Indefinite** | `will / shall + V1` | `will / shall + be + V3` | The bell **will be rung**. |\n| **10** | **Future Continuous** | `will be + V-ing` | *[Rare]* `will be being + V3` | *Avoided in standard English* |\n| **11** | **Future Perfect** | `will have + V3` | `will have been + V3` | The bell **will have been rung**. |\n| **12** | **Future Perfect Cont.** | `will have been + V-ing` | *[Rare]* `will have been being + V3` | *Avoided in standard English* |\n\n---\n\n### 👤 Pronoun Transformation Table\n\n| Subjective Case (Active Subject) | Objective Case (Passive Agent after 'by') |\n|---|---|\n| **I** | **me** |\n| **We** | **us** |\n| **You** | **you** |\n| **He** | **him** |\n| **She** | **her** |\n| **It** | **it** |\n| **They** | **them** |\n| **Who** | **whom** |\n\n---\n\n### 🔑 The 5 Golden Rules of Voice Transformation\n\n1. **The Object becomes the Subject:** Always locate the direct object first. If there is no object, verify whether the verb is intransitive.\n2. **Auxiliary 'Be' Matches the Tense:** The tense of the original active sentence is carried entirely by the auxiliary form of *to be*.\n3. **Past Participle (V3) is Universal:** The main verb in passive voice is *always* transformed into its 3rd form (past participle).\n4. **Preserve the Sentence Mood:** Assertives remain assertive; interrogatives remain interrogative; imperatives remain imperative.\n5. **Drop Unnecessary Agents:** When the subject is vague (*someone, somebody, people, they, one*), omit the *by-agent* phrase completely (*\"My purse was stolen\"*, not *\"by someone\"*).\n",
