      "duration": "25 mins",
      "type": "text",
      "content": "# 🟠 Past Indefinite Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + was / were + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nPast Indefinite (Simple Past) narrates completed actions at a definite time in the past. When reporting historical milestones, accidental events, or news incidents where the recipient takes center stage, Past Indefinite passive is the most frequently utilized construction in the English language.\n\n#### Auxiliary Selection:\n- **was:** Used with *I, He, She, It, singular noun*\n- **were:** Used with *You, We, They, plural nouns*\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + V2 + Object` | `Object + was/were + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + did + not + V1 + Object` | `Object + was/were + not + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Did + Subject + V1 + Object + ?` | `Was/Were + Object + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Did + Subject + not + V1 + Object + ?` | `Was/Were + Object + not + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** Quaid-e-Azam founded Pakistan in 1947.\n- **Passive:** Pakistan was founded by Quaid-e-Azam in 1947.\n- **Active:** The government inaugurated the new international airport yesterday.\n- **Passive:** The new international airport was inaugurated by the government yesterday.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The driver did not notice the red traffic signal.\n- **Passive:** The red traffic signal was not noticed by the driver.\n- **Active:** The investigators did not find any incriminating evidence.\n- **Passive:** No incriminating evidence was found by the investigators.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Did the police arrest the burglars last night?\n- **Passive:** Were the burglars arrested by the police last night?\n- **Active:** Did Thomas Edison invent the electric bulb?\n- **Passive:** Was the electric bulb invented by Thomas Edison?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Did she not sign the official contract?\n- **Passive:** Was the official contract not signed by her?\n- **Active:** Did they not invite the neighborhood residents?\n- **Passive:** Were the neighborhood residents not invited by them?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Did the letter written by him?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Was** the letter written by him?* (Never retain 'did' in passive voice).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The window broke by the boy.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The window **was broken** by the boy.* ('Was broken' indicates passive voice).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Three goals was scored by the striker.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *Three goals **were** scored by the striker.* (Plural object requires 'were').\n",
