      "content": "# 🟠 Past Perfect Tense in Passive Voice\n\n> **Rule:** `Object + had + been + Past Participle (V3) + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nThe Past Perfect Tense denotes an action that occurred and concluded before another point or action in the past (the \"past before the past\"). In passive voice, **had been** is applied universally across all subjects regardless of number or person.\n\n#### Universal Auxiliary:\nUnlike present tenses that split between *has* and *have*, the auxiliary **had been** is invariant:\n- Singular: *The task had been finished.*\n- Plural: *The tasks had been finished.*\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Sentence Structure Breakdown\n\n| Sentence Type | Active Voice Formula | Passive Voice Formula |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Subject + had + V3 + Object` | `Object + had + been + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Subject + had + not + V3 + Object` | `Object + had + not + been + V3 + by + Subject` |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Had + Subject + V3 + Object + ?` | `Had + Object + been + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Had + Subject + not + V3 + Object + ?` | `Had + Object + not + been + V3 + by + Subject + ?` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### ✅ Positive Conversions\n- **Active:** The rescue team had evacuated the residents before the river breached its banks.\n- **Passive:** The residents had been evacuated by the rescue team before the river breached its banks.\n- **Active:** Ali had locked all laboratory doors prior to leaving.\n- **Passive:** All laboratory doors had been locked by Ali prior to leaving.\n\n#### ❌ Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** The committee had not approved the budget before the fiscal year commenced.\n- **Passive:** The budget had not been approved by the committee before the fiscal year commenced.\n- **Active:** She had not submitted the manuscript before the publisher's deadline.\n- **Passive:** The manuscript had not been submitted by her before the publisher's deadline.\n\n#### ❓ Interrogative Conversions\n- **Active:** Had the scientists discovered the cure before the epidemic spread?\n- **Passive:** Had the cure been discovered by the scientists before the epidemic spread?\n- **Active:** Had the manager resolved the dispute before the board met?\n- **Passive:** Had the dispute been resolved by the manager before the board met?\n\n#### ❓➕ Interrogative Negative Conversions\n- **Active:** Had they not dispatched the goods prior to receiving the payment?\n- **Passive:** Had the goods not been dispatched by them prior to receiving the payment?\n- **Active:** Had he not informed the authorities before taking action?\n- **Passive:** Had the authorities not been informed by him before taking action?\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The match had won by Pakistan before sunset.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The match **had been won** by Pakistan before sunset.*\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The letters has been posted before noon yesterday.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *The letters **had been** posted before noon yesterday.* ('Has' cannot accompany past tense).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *Had been the patient examined before the doctor arrived?*\n  - ✅ **Right:** ***Had the patient been** examined before the doctor arrived?*\n",
