      "duration": "20 mins",
      "type": "text",
      "content": "# 🟠 Past Perfect Continuous: Passive Analysis\n\n> **Theoretical Formula:** `Object + had + been + being + V3 + (by + Subject)`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Conventional Usage\nLike its present counterpart, **Past Perfect Continuous Tense is conventionally avoided in the passive voice**.\n\n#### Linguistic Rationale:\nThe sequence **had been being** is awkward, repetitious, and redundant in rhythm:\n- *Active:* \"The team had been digging the well for two weeks before they struck water.\"\n- *Theoretical Passive:* \"The well **had been being dug** by the team for two weeks before they struck water.\"\n\n#### Academic & Professional Alternatives:\n1. **Retain Active Voice (Standard):** Keep the sentence active.\n2. **Convert to Past Perfect Passive:** *\"The well had been dug for two weeks before water was struck.\"*\n3. **Convert to Past Continuous Passive:** *\"The well was being dug by the team when water was struck.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Theoretical Structural Matrix\n\n| Sentence Type | Theoretical Passive Structure | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **✅ Positive** | `Object + had been being + V3` | The road **had been being repaired** for hours. |\n| **❌ Negative** | `Object + had not been being + V3` | The equipment **had not been being serviced** regularly. |\n| **❓ Interrogative** | `Had + Object + been being + V3 + ?` | **Had** the account **been being audited** before the discrepancy appeared? |\n| **❓➕ Interrog. Negative** | `Had + Object + not + been being + V3 + ?` | **Had** the vehicle **not been being maintained** properly? |\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *The speech had being delivered for an hour.* ('Had being' is ungrammatical).\n- ❌ **Stylistic Error:** Inserting 'had been being' in formal essays or business correspondence when active voice communicates the concept cleanly.\n",
