      "id": "les-14-18",
      "title": "Impersonal Passive & That-Clause Transformations",
      "duration": "25 mins",
      "type": "text",
      "content": "# 📰 Impersonal Passive & That-Clause Transformations\n\n> **Pattern 1:** `It + be + V3 (said / believed / reported) + that-clause`\n> **Pattern 2:** `Subject (of that-clause) + be + V3 + to-infinitive`\n\n---\n\n### 📖 Introduction & Concept\nIn academic writing, journalistic reporting, and formal discourse, statements containing cognitive or reporting verbs (*say, believe, think, consider, claim, report, know, expect, understand*) are often impersonalized to express public opinion or unverified intelligence without holding the writer directly accountable.\n\n- *Active:* \"People say that honesty is the best policy.\"\n- **Passive Pattern 1 (Introductory 'It'):**\n  - *\"It is said that honesty is the best policy.\"*\n- **Passive Pattern 2 (Personal Subject with 'to-infinitive'):**\n  - *\"Honesty is said to be the best policy.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Structural Transformation Matrix\n\n| Active Construction | Passive Pattern 1 (Introductory 'It') | Passive Pattern 2 (Infinitive Shift) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **People say that he is a genius.** | `It is said that he is a genius.` | `He is said to be a genius.` |\n| **People believed that the earth was flat.** | `It was believed that the earth was flat.` | `The earth was believed to be flat.` |\n| **Police report that he has escaped.** | `It is reported that he has escaped.` | `He is reported to have escaped.` |\n| **Experts expect the economy to grow.** | `It is expected that the economy will grow.` | `The economy is expected to grow.` |\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Advanced Infinitive Rules in Pattern 2:\n\n1. **Simultaneous Action (Present Infinitive):**\n   - Active: \"They believe she lives in Islamabad.\"\n   - Passive: *\"She is believed to live in Islamabad.\"*\n2. **Prior Action (Perfect Infinitive - 'to have + V3'):**\n   - Active: \"They say that he stole the antique necklace.\"\n   - Passive: *\"He is said **to have stolen** the antique necklace.\"*\n3. **Ongoing Action (Continuous Infinitive - 'to be + V-ing'):**\n   - Active: \"People believe he is writing a new memoir.\"\n   - Passive: *\"He is believed **to be writing** a new memoir.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Practical Examples\n\n#### 📰 News & Journalistic Usage\n- **Active:** Journalists report that the two foreign ministers have signed a ceasefire treaty.\n  - **Pattern 1:** It is reported that the two foreign ministers have signed a ceasefire treaty.\n  - **Pattern 2:** The two foreign ministers are reported to have signed a ceasefire treaty.\n- **Active:** Historians consider Babur to be a visionary strategist.\n  - **Pattern 1:** It is considered that Babur was a visionary strategist.\n  - **Pattern 2:** Babur is considered to be a visionary strategist.\n- **Active:** Scientists know that smoking damages pulmonary tissue.\n  - **Pattern 1:** It is known that smoking damages pulmonary tissue.\n  - **Pattern 2:** Smoking is known to damage pulmonary tissue.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Common Mistakes & Pitfalls\n\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *He is said that he is rich.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *He is said **to be** rich.* OR *It is said that he is rich.* (Do not mix Pattern 1 and 2).\n- ❌ **Wrong:** *He is reported to stole the money.*\n  - ✅ **Right:** *He is reported **to have stolen** the money.* (Prior past actions require perfect infinitive).\n",
